Overlay patch 0059 (D39): the "Outdated ROM Archives" check acts on the REAL archive.

Reported on OTA 1.1.0.1 (iPhone): the popup "Your ROM archives were created
with incompatible versions of Lighthouse. You will now be redirected to
re-extract them." appeared at EVERY launch; OK led straight into the game on
the old assets, no re-extraction, popup again next launch.

Root cause (two upstream bugs that only bite together on iOS):
1. RunExtract reads the version from the archive it LOCATES
   (DetectOTRVersion -> LocateFileAcrossAppDirs -> $HOME/Documents/bk.o2r),
   but deletes `std::filesystem::remove(archive)` with the BARE name
   "bk.o2r", i.e. relative to the process cwd. On desktop cwd is the install
   dir, so the two agree; an iOS app's cwd is "/", so remove() finds nothing,
   returns false (non-throwing overload) and the archive in Documents
   survives. PS_FILE_CHECK then sees it (AnyRomArchiveExists resolves via
   Documents) and goes straight to ES_VERIFY -> game boots on old assets.
2. The check itself is truthful: an archive extracted by an earlier build
   carries that build's portVersion (1.0.x from the 1.0.1-1.0.3 builds, or
   none at all), and upstream 1.1.0 compares major.minor, so it is genuinely
   outdated -- it just never gets regenerated, so the popup returns forever.
   A fresh 1.1.0 extraction stamps 1.1.0 and passes (verified on the sim).

This patch (src/port/Extractor/ExtractFlow.{h,cpp}, src/port/Engine.cpp):
- resolves each archive to the path the version was read from, only acts on
  it when it lives in the writable app dir (never the bundle), and MOVES it
  aside to `<name>.outdated` instead of deleting it, so nothing the user had
  is lost before a replacement exists; falls back to remove() only if the
  rename fails, and logs loudly if neither works;
- deletes the `.outdated` copy only once the run ends with an archive that
  passes the version check (fresh extraction verified);
- records one verdict line (archive path, archive version, build version,
  ok/outdated/none, what was done) and logs it after logging is initialised
  (RunExtract runs before InitLogging, so its SPDLOG lines never reach
  logs/Lighthouse.log): `LH_ARCHIVE ...`.
The rest of the flow is upstream's own: with the archive gone, PS_FILE_CHECK
offers "Generate one now?", PS_LOCAL finds the ROM the onboarding shell left
in Documents, and the existing extraction runs.

